Another bug: `finishAttack` for the player checks `if (this.state === 'idle') this.faceTowardNearest(300);` then calls `game.onPlayerAttackEnd`. Fine.

The armor branch on hit while state 'attack' keeps attack active — good. But `this.attack` was set to null at line 616 before this check! So if armored light hit during attack, `attack=null` but state remains 'attack', and baseUpdate will do nothing (attack null) leaving state stuck. Need to accept interrupting attack for armor? Simpler: for armor and not heavy, only preserve state if not attack; if attack, keep attack and don't null it. Restructure takeHit: don't null attack until determining stun.

Let me rewrite the takeHit middle section cleanly:

```js
const noStun = this.armor >= 1 && !def.heavy && !def.launch;
if (!noStun) {
  this.comboStep=0; ...; this.attack=null; this.queued=null;
}
...
if (def.launch) {...}
else if (noStun) {
  if (!['attack','dodge','special','hurt','down','dead'].includes(this.state)) this.state='idle';
} else {
  this.state='hurt'; ...
}
```

Also if hurt, cancel attack. Let me patch lines 606-632.

Also `this.vzWasHigh` remove.

Also note player won't have armor.

Patch.

