I accidentally wrote a label `irc: for (...)` inside manholes — labeled loop is valid JS? `irc: for` is a valid label syntax. But it's unnecessary and weird. Also `drawRain` ignores dt except parameter; fine.

Now game.js — the core. Let's design thoroughly.

```js
import { World } from './world.js';
import { Particles } from './particles.js';
import { Player... } from './fighters.js';
import { drawStickman, drawGroundShadow } from './stickman.js';
import { clamp, damp, lerp, rand, chance, formatScore, formatTime, pick } from './utils.js';

export class Game {
  constructor(canvas, ui, input, audio) {...}
  initMenuScene()
  start()
  restart()
  toMenu()
  resize()
  update(dt)
  render()
}
```

UI class separate; I'll implement ui.js after. Game expects UI methods.

Since game loop is in main.js, Game exposes update(dt) and render(). Input edge clearing in main.

Resize: canvas sizing with DPR (cap 2), W/H CSS px, s, baseline, depthPx. Also view.

```
resize() {
  const W = innerWidth, H = innerHeight;
  const dpr = Math.min(devicePixelRatio||1, 2);
  canvas.width = W*dpr; canvas.height = H*dpr; canvas.style.width = W+'px';...
  this.W=W; this.H=H; this.dpr=dpr;
  this.s = clamp(Math.min(W/1250, H/760), 0.5, 1.55);
  const touch = this.input.usingTouch || matchMedia(...).matches;
  this.baseline = H * (touch ? 0.62 : 0.70);
  this.depthPx = 150 * this.s;
  this.camX = clamp(this.camX, 0, WORLD_WIDTH);
}
```
Camera: `this.camX` target center; view width = W/s. Clamp center to [viewHalf, WORLD_WIDTH-viewHalf] if view width < world, else center.

Camera follow: target = player.x + facing*40; when enemies near, shift toward midpoint? Let's use player.x plus velocity look-ahead. Smooth damp 4. Clamp.

Trauma: addShake(amount) sets trauma = min(1, trauma+amount). decay ~1.6/s. Shake offset = trauma^2 * 16 * random, and rotation tiny. zoom = 1 + zoomPulse; zoomPulse decays.

Slowmo: timer and scale. During boss death, slowmo 1.2s with timeScale 0.3. Hitstop freezes simulation entirely but particles/camera update? I'll freeze fighters and effects for hitstop (like a frame), but update camera shake for feel. Implementation in update():
```
update(dt) {
  this.time += dt;
  if (this.state==='playing') {
    if (this.hitstop>0) { this.hitstop-=dt; this.updateCamera(dt,0); return; }
    const scale = this.slowmo>0 ? 0.35 : 1;
    this.slowmo = max(0, slowmo-dt);
    dt *= scale;
    ...
  }
}
```
Careful: using dt scaled for timers like slowmo countdown - countdown uses real dt. Save real dt.

Menu: state 'menu'; update demo actors; camera drift; particles update; world update. Render menu scene with demo fighters + title screen overlay.

Start: reset all, player created, enemies=[], waveIndex=-1; startWave(0); state='playing'; UI hide title, show HUD and touch; audio startMusic; hint display.

