Now, what about mobile page (second page in same browser)? Menu hidden for 1.6s; harness clicks at ~0.5s (warm); gameplay starts; fine.

The human UX: 1.6s of near-black background behind the title content. The title overlay left side is already 94% opaque at left; the right side reveals the scene. On desktop, for 1.6s the right side is dark; then the city appears. Acceptable but could look like a load. Maybe fade in the canvas with a CSS transition of opacity over 400ms when revealed; the first composite cost still occurs but after click. Use `.is-veiled{opacity:0}` and transition opacity .5s; but opacity:0 still composites? An opacity-0 layer may be skipped. Use both visibility and opacity.

